{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison","lean:module:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.Continuity","lean:module:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.LocalMonodromy","lean:module:QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjectorContinuity","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedding","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboActionKernel","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Matrix","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.NormedSpace.Connected","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.Module.Cardinality","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Complex.FiniteDimensional"],"declarations":61,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_complex_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_complex_σ","kind":"theorem","line":752,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L752-L764","doc":"**Generator form at a complex coupling.** If `q = e^{2πiκ}` is not a root of unity, one\ninvertible `U` satisfies `U · (e^{2πiκc} θ_κ(σ_j)) = Ř_{j,j+1}(q) · U` for every `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_complex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_complex","kind":"theorem","line":715,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L715-L750","doc":"**The Kohno comparison at every complex coupling `κ` with `q = e^{2πiκ}` not a root of\nunity.** The KZ representation of `H_{m+1}(q)` on `V^{⊗(m+1)}`, `V = ℂ²`, rescaled by\n`e^{2πiκc}` per crossing, is conjugate to Jimbo's by an invertible matrix. No separation\nhypothesis is needed: it follows from `q` not being a root of unity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHeckeC_zero_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHeckeC_zero_σ","kind":"theorem","line":708,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L708-L713","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_jimboRepC_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_jimboRepC_σ","kind":"theorem","line":702,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L702-L706","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_kzHeckeC_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_kzHeckeC_σ","kind":"theorem","line":688,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L688-L700","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHeckeC_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHeckeC_σ","kind":"theorem","line":681,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L681-L686","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHeckeC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHeckeC","kind":"def","line":675,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L675-L679","doc":"The KZ representation of `H_{m+1}(q(κ))` at a complex coupling `κ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzQuadC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzQuadC","kind":"theorem","line":665,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L665-L673","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.countable_rootOfUnity_couplings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.countable_rootOfUnity_couplings","kind":"theorem","line":647,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L647-L663","doc":"**The root-of-unity couplings are countable**: `q(κ)^k = 1` with `k > 0` forces `κ ∈ ℚ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_qC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_qC","kind":"theorem","line":644,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L644-L645","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qC_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qC_zero","kind":"theorem","line":642,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L642-L642","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qC_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qC_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":640,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L640-L640","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qC","kind":"def","line":637,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L637-L638","doc":"The Hecke parameter as a function of a complex coupling: `q(κ) = e^{2πiκ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_pos","kind":"theorem","line":614,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L614-L627","doc":"**The Kohno comparison at every real `q₀ > 0`.** At the coupling `κ₀ = ln q₀/(2πi)` the\nrescaled KZ generators on `V^{⊗(m+1)}` are simultaneously conjugate to Jimbo's `Ř(q₀)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_real","kind":"theorem","line":592,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L592-L612","doc":"**Kohno comparison at every real coupling `κ = t/(2πi)`, `t ∈ ℝ`** (every real `q = e^t > 0`):\nthe KZ representation of `H_{m+1}(q)` on `V^{⊗(m+1)}` is conjugate to Jimbo's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHeckeRep_conj_of_interval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHeckeRep_conj_of_interval","kind":"theorem","line":570,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L570-L590","doc":"Rigidity on a closed interval `S` through the base point `0`, given that the points with\n`t ≠ 0` are dense in `S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHeckeRep_zero_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHeckeRep_zero_σ","kind":"theorem","line":563,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L563-L568","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_kzHeckeRep_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_kzHeckeRep_σ","kind":"theorem","line":550,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L550-L561","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_pin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_pin","kind":"theorem","line":531,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L531-L542","doc":"**The Kohno comparison at a real pin `q₀ ≥ 1`.** At the coupling `κ₀ = ln q₀/(2πi)` the\nrescaled KZ generators on `V^{⊗(m+1)}` are simultaneously conjugate to Jimbo's `Ř(q₀)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qOf_log","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qOf_log","kind":"theorem","line":528,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L528-L529","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qOf_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qOf_mem","kind":"theorem","line":523,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L523-L526","doc":"Along the segment, `q` is real and lies in `[1, e^L]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.isPreconnected_kappa_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.isPreconnected_kappa_image","kind":"theorem","line":519,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L519-L521","doc":"The couplings form a preconnected set (the image of `[0, L]`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kappa_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kappa_eq","kind":"theorem","line":511,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L511-L517","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_σ'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_σ'","kind":"theorem","line":494,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L494-L503","doc":"**Generator form, unconditional.** For every `t ≥ 0` one invertible `U` conjugates every\nrescaled KZ generator to the Jimbo `Ř`-matrix: `U (e^{2πiκc} θ_κ(σ_j)) = Ř_{j,j+1}(q) U`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":479,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L479-L492","doc":"**Kohno comparison, unconditional, for all real couplings `κ = t/(2πi)`, `t ≥ 0`.**\nFor every number of strands `m + 1`, every Casimir shift `c ∈ ℂ` and every `t ≥ 0`, the KZ\nrepresentation of `H_{m+1}(q)`, `q = e^t`, on `V^{⊗(m+1)}`, `V = ℂ²`, is conjugate to the Jimbo\nrepresentation by an invertible matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHeckeRep_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHeckeRep_σ","kind":"theorem","line":472,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L472-L477","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHeckeRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHeckeRep","kind":"def","line":466,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L466-L470","doc":"The KZ representation through `H_{m+1}(q)`, `q = e^{2πiκ(t)}`, for every `t`:\n`σ_j ↦ e^{2πiκc} θ_κ(σ_j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzQuad_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzQuad_holds","kind":"theorem","line":458,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L458-L464","doc":"**H1 holds unconditionally.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo_σ","kind":"theorem","line":439,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L439-L451","doc":"**Generator form.** Under H1, at every `t ∈ [0, L]` there is one invertible `U` with\n`U · (e^{2πiκc} θ_κ(σ_j)) · U⁻¹ = Ř_{j,j+1}(q)` for every generator, `κ = t/(2πi)`, `q = e^t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kz_conj_jimbo","kind":"theorem","line":399,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L399-L437","doc":"**The assembled Kohno comparison on the real segment.** Fix `c ∈ ℂ` and `L ≥ 0`. Assume\nonly **H1**: along the couplings `κ(t) = t/(2πi)`, `t ∈ [0, L]`, the first KZ generator\nsatisfies the Hecke quadratic with `q = e^{t}` (gap 1). Then at every `t ∈ [0, L]` the KZ\nrepresentation of `H_{m+1}(e^t)` on `V^{⊗(m+1)}` is conjugate to the Jimbo representation by\nan invertible matrix.\n\nThe Wedderburn continuity and the base point at `q = 1` (gaps 2 and 3) are not hypotheses:\nthey are discharged by `JMProjectorContinuity` and `permRep_adjSwap`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHecke_zero_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHecke_zero_σ","kind":"theorem","line":389,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L389-L397","doc":"**The base point.** At `t = 0` (coupling `0`, `q = 1`) the KZ and Jimbo maps agree on the\ngenerators: both send `σ_j` to the permutation matrix of `(j, j+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_jimboRep_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_jimboRep_σ","kind":"theorem","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L383-L387","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuousOn_kzHecke_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuousOn_kzHecke_σ","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L369-L381","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHecke_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHecke_σ","kind":"theorem","line":361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L361-L367","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzHecke","kind":"def","line":353,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L353-L359","doc":"The KZ representation through `H_{m+1}(q)` along the segment (`σ_j ↦ e^{2πiκc} θ_κ(σ_j)`);\noff the segment it is set to the Jimbo map, which plays no role. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.KZQuad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.KZQuad","kind":"def","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L343-L351","doc":"**Hypothesis H1 (gap 1).** At coupling `κ(t)`, the first KZ generator on `m + 1` strands\n(with `ρ = permRep`, i.e. on `V^{⊗(m+1)}`, `V = ℂ²`), rescaled by `e^{2πiκc}`, satisfies the\nHecke quadratic with `q = e^{2πiκ}`. Proved for `m = 1` (`kzTwoStrand_isHeckeQuad`); open for\n`m ≥ 2`. This is exactly the shape of `KZTwoStrandHecke.kzTwoStrand_isHeckeQuad`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzScale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kzScale","kind":"def","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L340-L341","doc":"The scalar `s = e^{2πiκc}` by which each KZ crossing is rescaled. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_qOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_qOf","kind":"theorem","line":335,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L335-L336","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qOf_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qOf_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L329-L333","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qOf_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qOf_zero","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L327-L327","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qOf_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qOf_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L325-L325","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qOf_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qOf_eq","kind":"theorem","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L321-L323","doc":"**Along the segment the Hecke parameter is the positive real `e^t`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.qOf","kind":"def","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L318-L319","doc":"The Hecke parameter of the KZ representation at `κ(t)`: `q = e^{2πiκ(t)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_kappa","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L315-L316","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kappa_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kappa_zero","kind":"theorem","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L313-L313","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.two_kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.two_kappa","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L308-L311","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.kappa","kind":"def","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L305-L306","doc":"The KZ coupling along the segment: `κ(t) = t / (2πi)`, purely imaginary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.conj_of_isPreconnected_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.conj_of_isPreconnected_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L259-L292","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.rank_eq_of_intertwine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.rank_eq_of_intertwine","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L253-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.jimboRep_eq_jimbo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.jimboRep_eq_jimbo","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L229-L234","doc":"**`jimboRep` is the corpus's Jimbo action** `JimboActionKernel.jimbo` (`heckeActionN` read\nthrough the balanced-presentation bridge): both send `σ_j` to `Ř_{j,j+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.jimboRep_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.jimboRep_σ","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L225-L227","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.jimboRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.jimboRep","kind":"def","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L211-L223","doc":"**The Jimbo action** `H_{m+1}(q) →ₐ M_{2^{m+1}}(K)`, `σ_j ↦ Ř_{j,j+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.strandBraid_quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.strandBraid_quad","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L202-L209","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.permRep_adjSwap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.permRep_adjSwap","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L160-L188","doc":"**At `q = 1` the Jimbo generator is the permutation matrix of the adjacent transposition**,\nexactly (no scalar). This is the base-point match between KZ at coupling `0`\n(`kzBraidRep_zero_σ`) and Jimbo at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.permRep_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.permRep_apply","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L157-L158","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.permRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.permRep","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L141-L155","doc":"The permutation representation of `S_k` on `V^{⊗k}`, `V = R²`, in the coordinate model\n`(Fin k → Fin 2) → R`: `permRep σ a b = 1` iff `b = a ∘ σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_strandBraid_exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.continuous_strandBraid_exp","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L122-L131","doc":"**The Jimbo generator is continuous in the coupling.** With `q = e^z`, `z ∈ ℂ`\n(`z = 2πiκ` in the KZ normalisation), every entry is `0`, `1`, `q` or `q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.strandBraid_eq_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.strandBraid_eq_eval","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L110-L120","doc":"**The Jimbo generator is a Laurent-polynomial matrix in `q`.** For every unit `q` of a\ncommutative ring, `Ř_{j,j+1}(q, q⁻¹)` is the evaluation at `q` of the fixed matrix\n`Ř_{j,j+1}(T, T⁻¹)` over `R[T, T⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.strandBraid_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.strandBraid_map","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L105-L108","doc":"**The Jimbo generator commutes with change of coefficients.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.embedPair_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.embedPair_map","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L98-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.rCheck_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoAssembly.rCheck_map","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoAssembly.lean#L93-L96","signatureChunk":0}]}